    "The two εἰς + predicate nominal phrases were analysed alike under rule 24. Giving each εἰς the supplied 'a' was rejected: 'a Father' and 'a Son' are the indefinite determiners an anarthrous English count noun requires, and rule 51's anarthrous clause makes them helpers on the noun.",
